<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dimitrov Constitution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1947</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dimitrov Constitution was the constitution of the People's Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> adopted on 4 December 1947 and named after the communist leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgi-dimitrov">Georgi Dimitrov</a>. Modelled on the Soviet constitution of 1936, it proclaimed Bulgaria a people's republic, provided for the nationalisation of industry and banks and created a single-chamber National Assembly. It remained in force until it was replaced by a new constitution in 1971.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dimitrov-constitution.jpg" alt="Dimitrov Constitution" width="320" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Biser Todorov · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Constitution_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_Bulgaria_of_1947.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
